LXC Desktop Deployment Toolkit
==============================

This toolkit manages the deployment of X11-capable LXC containers with
GPU passthrough support. It handles:

  - Container configuration with proper cgroup device access rules
  - Device node creation for GPU, TTY, and input devices
  - Xorg configuration for containerized input handling
  - X server startup with dedicated display/VT allocation

Files:
  container.conf     - LXC container configuration
  setup-devices.sh   - Device node creation script (supports --dry-run)
  start-desktop.sh   - X11 session startup script
  xorg.conf.d/       - Xorg server configuration snippets
  deploy.sh          - Deployment validation and management

Usage:
  ./deploy.sh validate    - Check all configuration files for errors
  ./setup-devices.sh --dry-run  - Preview device setup commands
  ./start-desktop.sh      - Start the desktop session

Requirements:
  - LXC 5.0+ with cgroup2 support
  - NVIDIA GPU with driver 525+
  - Host kernel with /dev/input support
